{
  "name": "How to Prepare Your Home for a Professional Roof Inspection",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Clear the Perimeter and Access Points",
      "text": "Before the inspection, make sure the areas around your home, especially beneath the roofline and near any potential ladder access points, are clear. Move patio furniture, outdoor decorations, and anything else that might obstruct access or be in the way. This ensures the team can safely set up ladders and move around without any tripping hazards or damage to your belongings.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Secure Pets and Valuables Indoors",
      "text": "For the safety of your pets and the inspection team, it’s best to keep all animals securely inside or away from the property during the inspection. Also, if you have any fragile items directly beneath the roof inside your home, especially in attic spaces, you might want to move them just in case. While our team is careful, it's always better to be safe than sorry.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Provide Relevant Information",
      "text": "Gather any past roof inspection reports, repair records, or warranty information you might have. This background can give the inspectors a clearer picture of your roof's history and any recurring issues. Even noting down when your roof was last replaced or if you've noticed any specific leaks can be super helpful for a comprehensive assessment.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Ensure Interior Access (If Applicable)",
      "text": "Often, a thorough roof inspection includes checking the interior of your home for signs of leaks or moisture, particularly in the attic. Make sure access to these areas is clear. If you're going to be away, let the roofing company know in advance and arrange for access if an interior check is part of their process.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Ask Questions and Communicate Concerns",
      "text": "Don't hesitate to communicate any specific concerns or areas you've noticed yourself, like a drip or a strange sound after rain. Our team at Discounted Roofing Co. is here to provide clear answers and practical recommendations, so openly sharing your observations helps us ensure we cover everything. Clear communication leads to the best outcomes. When Professional Guidance Helps: Remember, if you're ever unsure about anything related to your roof's condition or the inspection process, that's when a professional really shines. Our team is experienced and knowledgeable, ready to guide you step by step through identifying potential issues and understanding your options. Don't let a small concern turn into a big headache.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
      "h1",
      ".howto-step",
      "[itemprop=\"step\"]"
    ]
  },
